  partName: Top Front Bolt
  description: The Top Front Bolt is a small, thin-flat bolt located at the top-center-front
    of the engine, constructed from Material.006, which secures the top front cover
    plate or other components in place. This bolt is essential for maintaining the
    engine's structural integrity, and a notable aspect is that it must be tightened
    to the recommended torque specification to prevent damage or leaks. The Top Front
    Bolt works in conjunction with other bolts to ensure a secure and reliable engine
    assembly.
